[Term]
id: CL:0020065
name: ionocyte of salivary gland
def: "An ionocyte that is part of a salivary gland, localized to the ductal compartment on the luminal side. This specialized epithelial cell is characterized by expression of FOXI1 and is involved in regulating and maintaining osmotic pressure within the glandular environment (Dong et al., 2024). In normal human salivary glands, FOXI1-positive cells constitute less than 5% of ductal epithelial cells and are found exclusively in ducts, never in acini, across all major gland types including parotid, submandibular, sublingual, and minor salivary glands (Hoki et al., 2024). Like ionocytes in other tissues, this cell is expected to express high levels of CFTR and possess abundant mitochondria and ion transporters." [PMID:30069044, PMID:30069046, PMID:38358561, PMID:39346911, PMID:41721487]
is_a: CL:0005006 ! ionocyte
intersection_of: CL:0005006 ! ionocyte
intersection_of: part_of UBERON:0001044 ! saliva-secreting gland
relationship: capable_of GO:0050801 ! monoatomic ion homeostasis
relationship: dc-contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5507-2103
relationship: part_of UBERON:0001044 ! saliva-secreting gland
relationship: term_tracker_item https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/3597
property_value: dcterms-date "2026-03-24T10:46:30Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: CL:0020066
name: myoepithelial cell of salivary gland
def: "A myoepithelial cell that is part of a salivary gland, positioned between the basal lamina and the secretory or ductal epithelial cells surrounding acini and intercalated ducts. This cell adopts a stellate morphology with four to eight cellular processes around acini and an elongated form parallel to the ductal axis around intercalated ducts (Amano et al., 2012). It expresses alpha-smooth muscle actin (ACTA2/alpha-SMA) as a primary marker, along with p63 and aquaporin 1 (AQP1), and contracts rhythmically in response to neural stimulation to facilitate saliva expulsion from secretory acini into the ductal system (Amano et al., 2012). This cell also produces FGF7, which activates FGFR2b-dependent transcriptional programs essential for seromucous acinar cell differentiation (Aure et al., 2023). In mice, myoepithelial cells express SOX2 and possess regenerative capacity, contributing to acinar cell restoration during tissue repair after severe injury." [PMID:23209333, PMID:39346911, PMID:40837863, PMID:41271704]
synonym: "basket cell of salivary gland" RELATED [PMID:26015726, PMID:27721614, PMID:38273256]
synonym: "salivary gland myoepithelial cell" EXACT [PMID:23209333, PMID:39346911, PMID:8155903]
synonym: "salivary myoepithelial cell" EXACT [PMID:40837863]
