[Term]
id: GO:0035846
name: oviduct epithelium development
def: "The progression of the oviduct epithelium over time from its initial formation to the mature structure. An oviduct is a tube through which an ova passes from the ovary to the uterus, or from the ovary to the outside of the organism. The oviduct epithelium is the specialized epithelium that lines the oviduct." [GOC:yaf, PMID:34496237]
