[Term]
id: GO:0072237
name: metanephric proximal tubule development
def: "The process whose specific outcome is the progression of the metanephric proximal tubule over time, from its formation to the mature structure. The metanephric proximal tubule is a metanephric nephron tubule that connects Bowman's capsule to the descending thin limb of the loop of Henle in the metanephros. It has a brush border epithelial morphology." [GOC:mtg_kidney_jan10]
