creation_date: 2010-03-18T03:50:29Z

[Term]
id: GO:0072243
name: metanephric nephron epithelium development
def: "The process whose specific outcome is the progression of the metanephric nephron epithelium over time, from its formation to the mature structure. An epithelium is a tissue that covers the internal or external surfaces of an anatomical structure. The metanephric nephron epithelium is a tissue that covers the surface of a nephron in the metanephros." [GOC:mtg_kidney_jan10]
