[Term]
id: GO:0072286
name: metanephric connecting tubule development
def: "The process whose specific outcome is the progression of the metanephric connecting tubule over time, from its formation to the mature structure. The metanephric connecting tubule is a tubular segment of the metanephric nephron; it connects the distal convoluted tubule to the collecting duct in the metanephros." [GOC:mtg_kidney_jan10]
