[Term]
id: UBERON:0000050
name: simple eye with multiple lenses
def: "Simple eye that has two or more lenses. Some marine organisms bear more than one lens; for instance the copeopod Pontella has three. The outer has a parabolic surface, countering the effects of spherical aberration while allowing a sharp image to be formed. Copilla's eyes have two lenses, which move in and out like a telescope." [Wikipedia:Eye#Multiple_lenses]
subset: grouping_class
subset: uberon_slim
xref: Wikipedia:Eye#Multiple_lenses
