property_value: external_comment "In some teleosts the anterior vertebral centra fuse to the basioccipital forming a monopartite occipital condyle.[TAO]" xsd:string {date_retrieved="2012-09-06", external_class="TAO:0000472", ontology="TAO", source="Curator"}
property_value: external_definition "An unpaired medial bone contributing to the ventral margin of the foramen magnum that extends into the floor of the brain cavity. It can contribute to the centromedial portion of the occipital condyle.[AAO]" xsd:string {date_retrieved="2012-06-20", external_class="AAO:0000039", ontology="AAO", source="AAO:EJS"}
property_value: external_definition "Chondral bone that articulates with the exoccipitals dorsally, the prootics anteriorly, the parasphenoid ventrally, and the first free vertebra posteriorly. The basioccipital forms the floor of the foramen magnum. The basioccipital is an unpaired medial bone.[TAO]" xsd:string {date_retrieved="2012-08-14", external_class="TAO:0000472", ontology="TAO", source="TAO:GA_TG"}

[Term]
id: UBERON:0001693
name: exoccipital bone
def: "Paired cartilage bone that bears a large foramen (lateral occipital foramen). Contacts the supraoccipital dorsally, the epiotic laterally and the basioccipital ventrally. Forms the posterior hind margin of the cranium and borders the lateral and posterior margins of the forum (foramen) magnum." [Wikipedia:Lateral_parts_of_occipital_bone, ZFIN:curator]
