[Term]
id: UBERON:0002233
name: tectorial membrane of cochlea
def: "The overlaying membrane of the cochlear duct, an extracellular matrix of the inner ear that contacts the stereocilia bundles of specialized sensory hair cells; sound induces movement of these hair cells relative to the tectorial membrane, deflects the stereocilia, and leads to fluctuations in hair cell membrane potential, transducing sound into electrical signals[MP,modified]." [J:77634, MGI:anna, MP:0003149]
subset: human_subset
subset: mouse_subset
subset: pheno_slim
subset: uberon_slim
