[Term]
id: UBERON:0005475
name: sigmoid sinus
def: "A portion of the lateral venous sinus, bulging prominently into the mastoid cavity, that serves as a principal conduit by which blood leaves the cranium[EPIC]. The sigmoid is drained by the internal jugular vein." [http://palaeos.com/vertebrates/glossary/glossaryS.html, Wikipedia:Sigmoid_sinus]
