id: UBERON:0005628
name: ileal artery
def: "The ileal arteries feed oxygenated blood into the ileum, a portion of the small intestine in mammals, reptiles, and birds. They are branches of the superior mesenteric artery." [Wikipedia:Ileal_arteries]
subset: human_reference_atlas
subset: human_subset
subset: mouse_subset
synonym: "arteriae ileales" RELATED OMO:0003011 [Wikipedia:Ileal_arteries]
