[Term]
id: UBERON:0006699
name: foramen cecum of tongue
def: "The median pit on the dorsum of the posterior part of the tongue, from which the limbs of a V-shaped furrow run forward and outward; the foramen cecum is the point of attachment of the thyroglossal duct and is formed during the embryological descent of the thyroid gland." [https://github.com/obophenotype/uberon/issues/281, MP:0013234]
