[Term]
id: UBERON:0007358
name: abomasum
def: "The fourth stomach of ruminating animals, which is an elongated pear-shaped sac lying on the floor of the abdomen, on the right-hand side, and roughly between the seventh and twelfth ribs. It leads to the beginning of the small intestine. (Adapted From Black's Veterinary Dictionary, 17th ed)." [MESH:A13.869.106, UBERON:cjm, Wikipedia:Abomasum]
