synonym: "suprangular" RELATED [https://github.com/obophenotype/uberon/issues/164, Wikipedia:Suprangular]
synonym: "suprangular bone" RELATED [https://github.com/obophenotype/uberon/issues/164]
synonym: "surangular" EXACT [TAO:0002287]
xref: http://palaeos.com/vertebrates/bones/dermal/images/Dentary1.gif
xref: http://palaeos.com/vertebrates/bones/dermal/images/Surangular1.gif
xref: TAO:0002287
is_a: UBERON:0004768 ! bone of lower jaw
is_a: UBERON:0008907 {source="Palaeos", source="TAO"} ! dermal bone
relationship: connected_to UBERON:0004744 ! articular/anguloarticular
relationship: part_of RO:0002577 ! system
relationship: part_of UBERON:0001710 ! lower jaw region
relationship: part_of UBERON:0003113 {notes="mandibular series", source="ISBN:0073040584"} ! dermatocranium
relationship: part_of UBERON:0003278 {source="paleos.com"} ! skeleton of lower jaw
property_value: external_definition "Dermal bone of the suspensorium.[TAO]" xsd:string {date_retrieved="2012-08-14", external_class="TAO:0002287", ontology="TAO", source="TAO:wd"}
property_value: taxon_notes "In some lepospondyls, and in frogs and salamanders, the surangular is absent. However, it becomes increasingly significant in the anthracosaur lineage. In turtles, it is one of the two principle bones of the lower jaw. In lepidosaurs, it is less important because of the development of a separate coronoid bone. In advanced lizards and pythonomorphs, it may fuse with the articular and perhaps other bones and loses its separate identity. In syanapsids, a secondary jaw joint develops between the surangular and the squamosal, which becomes the unique mammalian jaw articulation. However, the surangular fuses with the dentary and becomes the unitary mammalian 'mandible' without a separate identity" xsd:string
property_value: taxon_notes "Nevertheless, it is not completely clear that this[osteichthyans] surangular is homologous with the surangular in tetrapods" xsd:string {source="paleos"}

