[Term]
id: UBERON:0011794
name: rectrix feather
def: "A flight feather that lies along a single horizontal row on the rear margin of the anatomical tail. Only the central pair are attached (via ligaments) to the tail bones; the remaining rectrices are embedded into the rectricial bulbs, complex structures of fat and muscle that surround those bones. Rectrices are always paired, with a vast majority of species having six pairs. They are absent in grebes and some ratites, and greatly reduced in size in penguins." [Wikipedia:Flight_feather#Rectrices]
synonym: "rectrices" EXACT OMO:0003004 []
