subset: mouse_subset
synonym: "sphincter colli" EXACT []
is_a: UBERON:0002377 ! muscle of neck
property_value: structure_notes "The m. sphincter in the head region can be divided into 2 layers: M. sphincter colli profundus and superficialis; in studied placentals, the deepest layer has circular fibers, while the superficial layer has oblique and longitudinal fibers. In non-mammalian vertebrates (if differentiated) and in monotremes both the superficialis and the profundus layers are circular ('sphincter') muscles (Shumacher, 1956; Saban, 1971)." xsd:string {source="MorphoBank"}

