[Term]
id: UBERON:0018109
name: anterior auricular muscle
def: "The anterior auricular muscle, the smallest of the three auriculares muscles, is thin and fan-shaped, and its fibers are pale and indistinct. It arises from the lateral edge of the galea aponeurotica, and its fibers converge to be inserted into a projection on the front of the helix." [Wikipedia:Anterior_auricular_muscle_muscle]
