def: "A zone of bone organ located on the inferior articular process of the twelfth thoracic vertebra. T12 is the most transitional thoracic vertebra; its inferior articular facets face laterally, closely resembling the lumbar pattern, and articulate with the superior articular facets of L1 at the thoracolumbar junction." [https://fipat.library.dal.ca/ta2/, ISBN:9780323393225, Wikipedia:Thoracic_vertebrae]
