[Term]
id: UBERON:1200130
name: mammillary process of first lumbar vertebra
def: "A process of vertebra located on the posterior surface of the superior articular process of the first lumbar vertebra, presenting as a small bony tubercle. It serves as an attachment site for the multifidus muscle and marks the most superior of the lumbar mammillary processes, situated just below the thoracolumbar junction." [https://fipat.library.dal.ca/ta2/, ISBN:9780323393225, Wikipedia:Lumbar_vertebrae]
