[Term]
id: UBERON:1200227
name: superior articular facet of eleventh thoracic vertebra
def: "A zone of bone organ located on the superior articular process of the eleventh thoracic vertebra, oriented in the coronal plane and facing posteriorly. It articulates with the inferior articular facet of T10 at the zygapophyseal joint; T11 is a transitional vertebra where facet morphology begins the shift toward the lumbar sagittal pattern." [https://fipat.library.dal.ca/ta2/, ISBN:9780323393225, Wikipedia:Thoracic_vertebrae]
