name: supinator fossa of ulna
def: "A bone fossa forming the concave depression on the lateral aspect of the proximal ulna, just distal to the radial notch, providing the origin for the deep fibres of the supinator muscle." [https://fipat.library.dal.ca/ta2/, ISBN:9780323393225, Wikipedia:Ulna]
