[Term]
id: UBERON:1200269
name: transverse costal facet of fourth thoracic vertebra
def: "A zone of bone organ located on the anterior surface of the transverse process of the fourth thoracic vertebra, presenting as a smooth concave articular area that articulates with the tubercle of the fourth rib at the costotransverse joint. Together with the body demifacets it completes the bony articulation of rib 4 with the thoracic column." [https://fipat.library.dal.ca/ta2/, ISBN:9780323393225, Wikipedia:Thoracic_vertebrae]
