[Term]
id: UBERON:1200292
name: vertebral arch of fifth thoracic vertebra
def: "A neural arch forming the posterior bony ring of the fifth thoracic vertebra, consisting of pedicles and laminae that together with the body enclose the spinal canal at mid-thoracic level. Its spinous process is long and steeply inclined inferiorly, and the transverse processes project posterolaterally bearing facets for the tubercle of rib 5." [https://fipat.library.dal.ca/ta2/, ISBN:9780323393225, Wikipedia:Thoracic_vertebrae]
