[Term]
id: UBERON:1200299
name: vertebral arch of second cervical vertebra
def: "A neural arch forming the posterior bony ring of the axis (C2), composed of two robust pedicles and two broad laminae; it bears the characteristically large bifid spinous process posteriorly and supports the superior articular processes that articulate with the atlas." [https://fipat.library.dal.ca/ta2/, ISBN:9780323393225, Wikipedia:Axis_(anatomy)]
