name: vertebral arch of sixth thoracic vertebra
def: "A neural arch forming the posterior bony ring of the sixth thoracic vertebra, comprising paired pedicles and broad laminae enclosing the vertebral foramen. Located near the thoracic kyphotic apex, it bears a long, inferiorly inclined spinous process and transverse processes with costal facets that articulate with the tubercle of the sixth rib." [https://fipat.library.dal.ca/ta2/, ISBN:9780323393225, Wikipedia:Thoracic_vertebrae]
