[Term]
id: UBERON:2005259
name: continuous capillary
def: "Capillary that has endothelial cells that provide an uninterrupted lining, and only allow small molecules, like water and ions to diffuse through tight junctions which leave gaps of unjoined membrane which are called intercellular clefts." [Wikipedia:Capillary#Types]
subset: human_subset
subset: mouse_subset
synonym: "continuous blood vessel endothelium" BROAD []
synonym: "continuous blood vessel endothelium" EXACT [ZFA:0005259]
synonym: "continuous capillary vessel" EXACT [FMA:63195]
