name: fluid of fallopian tube ampulla
def: "A bodily fluid that fills the lumen of the fallopian tube ampulla, providing the aqueous medium in which fertilization occurs and through which the oocyte and sperm move." [https://purl.org/ccf/ASCTB-TEMP_fluid-of-fallopian-tube-ampulla, PMID:33167378, PMID:34496720]
subset: added_by_HRA
subset: human_subset
subset: mouse_subset
xref: Wikipedia:Ampulla_of_uterine_tube
is_a: UBERON:0006314 ! bodily fluid
relationship: dc-contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2999-0103
relationship: part_of UBERON:0012648 ! ampulla of fallopian tube
relationship: present_in_taxon NCBITaxon:9606 ! Homo sapiens
property_value: dcterms-date "2026-05-25T00:00:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: UBERON:8930042
name: fluid of fallopian tube fimbria
def: "A bodily fluid that is located in or secreted by the fimbria of the fallopian tube, which may facilitate the capture and transport of the ovum from the ovary into the oviduct." [https://purl.org/ccf/ASCTB-TEMP_fluid-of-fallopian-tube-fimbria, PMID:25994820]
subset: added_by_HRA
subset: human_subset
subset: mouse_subset
is_a: UBERON:0006314 ! bodily fluid
