relationship: present_in_taxon NCBITaxon:9606 ! Homo sapiens
property_value: dcterms-date "2026-05-25T00:00:00Z" xsd:dateTime

[Term]
id: UBERON:8930047
name: inner muscle layer of fallopian tube infundibulum
def: "An organ component layer composed primarily of circularly arranged smooth muscle tissue that forms the innermost layer of the muscular coat of the uterine tube infundibulum, contributing to peristaltic contractions that assist in gamete and embryo transport." [https://purl.org/ccf/ASCTB-TEMP_inner-muscle-layer-of-fallopian-tube-infundibulum, PMID:25866566, PMID:27875265]
