[Term]
id: UBERON:8930050
name: intramural segment of fallopian tube
def: "A subdivision of the fallopian tube that lies within the myometrium, the muscular wall of the uterus, connecting the isthmus to the uterine cavity. This is the narrowest and shortest segment of the fallopian tube, measuring approximately 0.7 mm in diameter and 1 cm in length." [https://purl.org/ccf/ASCTB-TEMP_intramural-segment-of-fallopian-tube, PMID:2565256, Wikipedia:Fallopian_tube]
subset: added_by_HRA
subset: human_subset
subset: mouse_subset
