[Term]
id: UBERON:8930077
name: outer muscle layer of fallopian tube ampulla
def: "A longitudinal smooth muscle layer that is part of the muscle coat of the ampulla of the fallopian tube. This layer forms the outermost component of the muscularis and works in coordination with the inner circular layer to produce the peristaltic movements necessary for transporting the oocyte and early embryo toward the uterus." [https://purl.org/ccf/ASCTB-TEMP_outer-muscle-layer-of-fallopian-tube-ampulla, PMID:1964529, PMID:2409745]
