[Term]
id: UBERON:8930193
name: inner periarterial lymphatic sheath of spleen
def: "The central region of the periarterial lymphatic sheath of the spleen, immediately surrounding the central arteriole. It forms the thymus-dependent (T cell) area of the splenic white pulp, is largely devoid of reticulum cells, and contains interdigitating cells in close contact with T lymphocytes." [DOI:10.1002/ar.1092320103, DOI:10.1007/BF00217084, DOI:10.1007/BF00225103]
comment: Inner/outer PALS subdivision is described in rat and mouse (Veerman & van Ewijk 1975, doi:10.1007/BF00225103). In adult human spleen the T-cell regions are discontinuous and lack rodent-type PALS architecture (van Krieken et al. 1985, doi:10.1111/j.1365-2559.1985.tb02841.x; Steiniger, Rüttinger & Barth 2003, doi:10.1177/002215540305100511); no inner/outer subdivision has been demonstrated in humans.
subset: added_by_HRA
subset: human_subset
subset: mouse_subset
synonym: "central PALS" EXACT [DOI:10.1007/BF00225103]
synonym: "inner PALS" EXACT [DOI:10.1007/BF00217084]
synonym: "inner periarterial lymphatic sheath" EXACT []
